 ### `$URL()`
 
-### `cleanDoubleSlashes(input)`
+### `cleanDoubleSlashes(input, respectQueryAndFragment?)`
 
 Removes double slashes from the URL.
 
+If second argument is `true`, the query and fragment are left untouched.
+
 **Example:**
 
 ```js
 cleanDoubleSlashes("//foo//bar//"); // "/foo/bar/"
 
+cleanDoubleSlashes("/foo//bar?redirect=//baz", true); // "/foo/bar?redirect=//baz"
+
 cleanDoubleSlashes("http://example.com/analyze//http://localhost:3000//");
 // Returns "http://example.com/analyze/http://localhost:3000/"
 ```
